WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.458
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
This week, we're

00:00:01.458 --> 00:00:03.720
talking about the PerfKit
Benchmarker, Kubernetes

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.570
updates, and new table
formats for Dataproc.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.240
I am Priyanka Vergadia,
and welcome to "This Week

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.710
in Cloud," where we serve
you the lowest-latency news.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:16.110
We've just expanded PerfKit
Benchmarker, the open source

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:19.320
tool that makes network
performance benchmarking faster

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.530
and easier.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.370
PerfKit Benchmarker now
supports a broader range

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.320
of network performance
tests and lets

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.620
you view the results
in Google Data Studio.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.140
The goal is to help you
predict the performance

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.790
impact of moving workloads to
and across different clouds.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:40.680
As Google Kubernetes Engine
moved from version 1.12 to 1.15

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.920
over the past year, we made
several security changes

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.340
to the platform to improve
security behind the scenes--

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.080
changes like paring
down controls

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.200
to only what your
application actually needs,

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.080
and improving the defaults,
and, of course, maintaining

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.080
the "GKE Hardening Guide"
so that you can always

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.440
find the best advice for the
security of your clusters.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.360
And speaking of
Kubernetes, it's never

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.210
a bad time for a Kubernetes
best practices guide.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:09.300
This one covers Kubernetes
namespaces, readiness probes

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.820
for health checks,
controlled deployment,

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.300
and more, because
containerized app management is

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.850
a favorite of ours for
deploying and managing

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.460
production apps at scale.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.650
Dataproc is a
fully-managed service

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.700
for running Apache
Hadoop ecosystem

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:29.040
software in the cloud, and we've
just added new table formats

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.490
to support workloads that
need ACID transactions, data

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:36.210
versioning, schema enforcement,
and schema evolution.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:38.310
Check out our new
guide on these formats,

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:40.110
and let us know what you think.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.600
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:45.120
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.430
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:51.050
We will see you in the cloud.

